codex
The core bridge and UI are now written: the hook gates only eligible foreground/default-mode calls, publishes capped previews, polls under the 20-second ceiling, and emits a decision only after validating it. The app now watches pending files, overlays `needs_me`, expands programmatically, renders the reference-style card, writes atomic decisions, and pulses `Approve?`; I’m doing a static audit next, especially for shell portability and Swift actor/isolation issues, without building or testing.
